    "narrative": "For today\u2019s matchup against a slate of mostly right-handed arms, the Zurich Zebras are prioritizing top-of-the-order stability and high-floor matchups. Our strongest play is **Christian Yelich** (75.84), who benefits significantly from the 5.17 xERA of Imai. With a massive +13% boost from his dynamic platoon advantage and a premium leadoff spot, he is our primary engine for runs today. Following closely is **Junior Caminero** (73.34), who continues to thrive in favorable hitting conditions against Kochanowicz. Both **Casey Schmitt** (63.92) and **Colt Keith** (63.27) also clear the 60-point threshold comfortably, fueled by the aggressive leadoff placement and favorable matchups that enhance their baseline production.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Chase Meidroth** (50.42), who was the first player cut from the active rotation. While he holds a respectable projection against Montero, the optimizer opted for the higher-ceiling profiles of **Gary Sanchez** and **Luke Raley** to ensure we maintain our competitive edge in the HR and RBI categories. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Trea Turner** (53.46) and **Kyle Schwarber** (54.85); while both are must-starts in most formats, they face the stiffest test of the day against Yamamoto. Their scores are artificially suppressed by the elite pitcher skill, though we expect the wind blowing out to provide a much-needed variance boost. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** remains a high-variance play; his score of 57.16 is tempered by a significant platoon disadvantage against Liberatore, but his elite sprint speed makes him an essential hold in our roster construction to bolster our scarcity-driven stolen base targets.",
